</element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig position="float" id="f1-medscimonit-17-7-cq3"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Fluoroscopy shows the femoro-femoral loop. The transseptal sheath crossing through the paravalvular leak from the left atrium into the left ventricle. The steerable electrode in transseptal sheath and Amplatz left catheter with a wire create the loop. Arrows show: 1 &#x02013; TEE transducer, 2 &#x02013; arterial catheter, 3 &#x02013; transseptal sheath, 4 &#x02013; ring of implanted mitral valve.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="medscimonit-17-7-cq3-g001" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="f2-medscimonit-17-7-cq3"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Fluoroscopy shows the distal disc opened in the left ventricle. The wire is released. The steerable electrode and the Amplatz catheter are removed. Through the transseptal sheath, an Amplatzer Vascular Plug III is advanced into the left ventricle. Arrows show: 1 &#x02013; TEE transducer, 2 &#x02013; transseptal sheath (advanced via PVL into the left ventricle), 3 &#x02013; ring of implanted mitral valve, 4 &#x02013; opened distal disc of the Amplatzer device.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="medscimonit-17-7-cq3-g002" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="f3-medscimonit-17-7-cq3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Fluoroscopy shows opened distal and proximal discs. The device is positioned into the leak and is detached from the guidewire. Arrows show: 1 &#x02013; TEE transducer, 2 &#x02013; Amplatzer Vascular Plug deployed in PVL, 3 &#x02013; transseptal sheath, 4 &#x02013; ring of implanted mitral valve.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="medscimonit-17-7-cq3-g003" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="f4-medscimonit-17-7-cq3"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Transthoracic echocardiogram (TTE), parasternal long axis view. The Amplatzer Vascular Plug III positioned in dehiscence (arrow). LV &#x02013; left ventricle, LA &#x02013; left atrium, RV &#x02013; right ventricle, Ao &#x02013; aorta.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="medscimonit-17-7-cq3-g004" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="f5-medscimonit-17-7-cq3"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Transthoracic echocardiogram (TTE) with color Doppler imagination, parasternal long axis view. The Amplatzer Vascular Plug III positioned in dehiscenece (arrow). No paravalvular leak shown in color Doppler imagination. LV &#x02013; left ventricle, RV &#x02013; right ventricle, La &#x02013; left atrium, Ao &#x02013; aorta.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="medscimonit-17-7-cq3-g005" position="float"/></fig></floats-group></article>